    "content": "{\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"content\": \"#include <stdio.h>\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\n#include <string.h>\\n#include <math.h>\\n\\n#define N_ITER 10 // number of simulation iterations\\n#define DT 0.01f // time step\\n#define SOFTENING 1e-9f // to avoid zero divisors\\n\\n/*\\n * Each body holds coordinate positions (i.e., x, y, and z) and\\n * velocities (i.e., vx, vy, and vz).\\n */\\ntypedef struct { float x, y, z, vx, vy, vz; } Body;\\n\\n/*\\n * Read a binary dataset with initilized bodies.\\n */\\nBody* read_dataset(int *nbodies) {\\n  int b = fread(nbodies, sizeof(*nbodies), 1, stdin);\\n  if (b != 1) {\\n    fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nError reading nbodie value\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n  }\\n  Body *bodies = (Body *)malloc(*nbodies * sizeof(Body));\\n  b = fread(bodies, *nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdin);\\n  if (b != 1) {\\n    fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nError reading input values\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n  }\\n\\n  return bodies;\\n}\\n\\n/*\\n * Write simulation results into a binary dataset.\\n */\\nvoid write_dataset(const int nbodies, Body *bodies) {\\n  int b = fwrite(bodies, nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdout);\\n  if (b != 1) {\\n    fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nError writing to output\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nint main(int argc,char **argv) {\\n  int nbodies;\\n\\n  Body *bodies = read_dataset(&nbodies);\\n\\n  /*\\n   * At each simulation iteration, interbody forces are computed,\\n   * and bodies' positions are integrated.\\n   */\\n  for (int iter = 0; iter < N_ITER; iter++) {\\n    #pragma omp parallel\\n    {\\n      // Force computation: dynamic scheduling balances load while preserving\\n      // per-body accumulation order (each i is handled by one thread).\\n      #pragma omp for schedule(dynamic,16)\\n      for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\\n        float fx = 0.0f;\\n        float fy = 0.0f;\\n        float fz = 0.0f;\\n\\n        for (int j = 0; j < nbodies; j++) {\\n          float dx = bodies[j].x - bodies[i].x;\\n          float dy = bodies[j].y - bodies[i].y;\\n          float dz = bodies[j].z - bodies[i].z;\\n          float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\\n          float inv_dist = 1 / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\\n          float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\\n\\n          fx += dx * inv_dist3;\\n          fy += dy * inv_dist3;\\n          fz += dz * inv_dist3;\\n        }\\n\\n        bodies[i].vx += DT*fx;\\n        bodies[i].vy += DT*fy;\\n        bodies[i].vz += DT*fz;\\n      }\\n\\n      // Position update: static schedule is sufficient and avoids extra overhead.\\n      #pragma omp for schedule(static)\\n      for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\\n        bodies[i].x += bodies[i].vx * DT;\\n        bodies[i].y += bodies[i].vy * DT;\\n        bodies[i].z += bodies[i].vz * DT;\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  write_dataset(nbodies, bodies);\\n\\n  free(bodies);\\n\\n  exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);\\n}\\n\",\n      \"path\": \"src/nbody.c\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Combining dynamic scheduling (chunk=16) on the force-computation outer loop with a static-scheduled position-update workshare inside one OpenMP parallel region per iteration may reduce load imbalance and thread-team creation overhead while preserving bitwise-identical output, because each body's inner accumulation order remains unchanged.\",\n  \"notes\": \"The force loop uses schedule(dynamic,16) to improve cache behavior and balance; the position update is statically scheduled. A single parallel region per iteration avoids repeated team creation for the two worksharing loops. All floating-point operations for a given i are performed by one thread in the original j order, so output bytes match the sequential reference exactly.\",\n  \"sources_kept\": [],\n  \"transformations\": [\n    \"Inlined body_force into main and added #pragma omp parallel around each iteration\",\n    \"Added #pragma omp for schedule(dynamic,16) to force computation loo